        <localActions>
            <fullName>get_funding_context_179We000000q4XP</fullName>
            <description>Traces the funding lineage/relationships around a starting point and returns a decision-ready summary. Two directions: (1) a Budget Line scope (country + business unit, optionally fiscal year and the cost dimensions) returns what funds it — the linked allocations, restrictions, gift commitments, opportunities and donors, with headroom and competing insight; (2) a named grant (opportunityName) returns where that grant&apos;s funding is allocated — the Budget Lines it funds, using allocation amounts, not the whole opportunity amount. Reports missing links (e.g. no gift commitment) instead of guessing.</description>
            <developerName>get_funding_context_179We000000q4XP</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeGetFundingContext</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>get_funding_context</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Get Funding Context</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>get_opportunity_context_179We000000q4XP</fullName>
            <description>Resolves a named grant&apos;s eligible country and program from its Restriction, plus the year, so a competing-grants analysis can run off it. Returns found=true with a single country and program only when the grant resolves to exactly one of each; otherwise found=false and the summary asks which to use.</description>
            <developerName>get_opportunity_context_179We000000q4XP</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeGetOpportunityContext</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>get_opportunity_context</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Get Opportunity Context</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>analyze_opportunity_competition_179We000000q4XP</fullName>
            <description>Opportunity-start competition. Given a grant name, finds the Budget Lines its allocations touch, determines the governed Headroom scopes those belong to, and reports the OTHER opportunities competing for the same governed headroom in EACH scope (a multi-scope grant is analyzed per scope, never collapsed), with the focus grant&apos;s exposure per scope and clickable record links. Returns found=false when the grant is not found, is ambiguous, or has no allocations tied to a governed Budget Line.</description>
            <developerName>analyze_opportunity_competition_179We000000q4XP</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeOpportunityCompetition</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>analyze_opportunity_competition</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Analyze Opportunity Competition</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>find_competing_grants_179We000000q4XP</fullName>
            <description>Governed competing-grants analysis. Resolves the SAME governed Budget Line population Headroom Analysis uses (Headroom category/program + country + fiscal year), aggregates the governed Headroom fields across all qualifying Budget Lines, then reports the Opportunities competing for that population by allocation EXPOSURE (not Opportunity Amount), split by Secured/Likely/Pipeline, with clickable Salesforce record links, a closing scenario, and severity (No Material / Moderate / High / Critical). Returns found=false for a governed-zero category, a not-yet-configured category, no qualifying lines, or a missing category/country.</description>
            <developerName>find_competing_grants_179We000000q4XP</developerName>
            <invocationTarget>AmaizeFindCompetingGrants</invocationTarget>
            <invocationTargetType>apex</invocationTargetType>
            <isConfirmationRequired>false</isConfirmationRequired>
            <isIncludeInProgressIndicator>false</isIncludeInProgressIndicator>
            <localDeveloperName>find_competing_grants</localDeveloperName>
            <masterLabel>Find Competing Grants</masterLabel>
        </localActions>
